message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Goldbach numbers in intervals of length log² x"
authors:
  - family-names: Vynohradov
    given-names: Anton
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-6771-3681"
version: "0.6"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24441477
date-released: 2026-11-24
license: MIT
type: software
abstract: >-
  Conditional on the Riemann hypothesis, every interval (x, x + log² x] with x ≥ r = 4.0462…
  (r + log² r = 6) contains a Goldbach number; the starting point is sharp, and 2/log² 4 = 1.0406…
  is the optimal constant on x ≥ 4 (previous constants: 123 published, 4.45 announced, 2 in v0.5).
  Paper, interval-arithmetic checks, and a conditional Lean 4 formalization. Unreviewed preprint,
  prepared with AI assistance.
